  "text": "[]>(\n\nBeginInitnings:\n\n1. Calculate the prime factorization of 2025.\n2. Determine the number of positive divisors of 2025.\n3. Calculate the probability that a randomly selected subset \\( B \\) of \\( A \\) has the property that the least common multiple (LCM) of its elements is 2025.\n4. Simplify the fraction to its lowest terms and find \\( m \\) and \\( n \\).\n5. Find the sum \\( m + n \\).\n\nStep 1: Prime factorization of 2025\n\nThe prime factorization of 2025 is:\n\\[ 2025 = 3^4 \\times 5^2 \\]\n\nStep 2: Number of positive divisors of 2025\n\nThe number of divisors of a number \\( n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\) is given by:\n\\[ (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1) \\]\nFor 2025, this is:\n\\[ (4 + 1)(2 + 1) = 5 \\times 3 = 15 \\]\nSo, \\( |A| = 15 \\).\n\nStep 3: Probability calculation\n\nA subset \\( B \\) of \\( A \\) will have the property that the LCM of its elements is 2025 if and only if each element of \\( B \\) is a divisor of 2025. The total number of subsets of \\( A \\) is \\( 2^{15} \\).\n\nThe number of subsets where the LCM is not 2025 is the number of subsets where at least one element is not a divisor of 2025. The number of elements not in \\( A \\) is 15 (since 2025 has 15 divisors). The number of subsets of these 15 elements is \\( 2^{15} \\). However, we must subtract the empty set, so the number of non-empty subsets where the LCM is not 2025 is \\( 2^{15} - 1 \\).\n\nThe number of subsets where the LCM is 2025 is \\( 2^{15} - (2^{15} - 1) = 2^{15} - 2^{15} + 1 = 1 \\) (the subset consisting of all elements of \\( A \\)).\n\nSo, the probability is:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{2^{15}} = \\frac{1}{32768} \\]\n\nStep 4: Simplify the fraction\n\nThe fraction \\( \\frac{1}{32768} \\) is already in its simplest form, with \\( m = 1 \\) and \\( n = 32768 \\).\n\nStep 5: Sum \\( m + n \\)\n\n\\[ m + n = 1 + 32768 = 32769 \\]\n\nFinal answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{32769}\n\\]",
